title: Shadows, weather and screen effects
intro: Lights now cast shadows, weather fills the sky, and the camera can make the whole screen look like an old TV or a handheld.
project: TopDown | Storm Keep

chapter: Shadows | Light, Shadows
say: The Top-down template is a dark dungeon, lit by torches and the player's lantern.
select: Main Camera
say: First, let's give the floor the color of stone, so we can see where the light falls.
set: Camera.Background = #6E685C
select: Player
explain: field:Light.Shadows | Shadows | Lights have a new setting, Shadows. With it ticked, walls, solid tiles and anything solid block the light and cast a shadow behind them.
say: The template's lantern and torches have it on. What carries the light, here the player, never gets in its way.
play
wait: 1
hold: Down 0.6
wait: 0.5
say: Walk past the crate, and its shadow swings away from the lantern.
hold: Left 1.2
wait: 0.4
hold: Right 2.2
wait: 0.8
say: Scripts see shadows too. Game dot Light At says how lit a spot is, so a stealth game's guards can't see you behind a pillar.
wait: 1
stop

chapter: Weather | Entity, Lights and Effects, Weather
create: Weather
explain: component:Weather | Weather | Weather, under Lights and Effects, makes rain, snow, falling leaves or rising embers that fill the view wherever the camera goes.
set: Weather.Amount = 0.8
set: Weather.Wind = -4
explain: field:Weather.Wind | Wind | Amount says how heavy it is, and Wind slants the rain and drifts the snow.
play
wait: 2
hold: Right 1.5
wait: 1
say: In the dark it's lit like everything else, so the rain glints near the lantern.
wait: 1
stop
set: Weather.Kind = Snow
set: Weather.Wind = 1
say: Switch it to snow.
play
wait: 3.5
stop
set: Weather.Kind = Rain
set: Weather.Storm = true
pick: Weather.ThunderSound = Sounds/explode.wav
explain: field:Weather.Storm | Storm | Tick Storm for lightning that flashes every few seconds, with thunder rumbling a moment later.
play
wait: 9
stop

chapter: Screen effects | Add Screen Effects to the camera
select: Main Camera
browse: ScreenEffects
explain: catalog:docs | Screen Effects | The new Screen Effects component changes the look of the whole screen, HUD included. It goes on the camera.
click: catalog:add
explain: component:ScreenEffects | A soft vignette | It starts with a soft vignette round the edges.
set: ScreenEffects.Scanlines = 0.6
set: ScreenEffects.Curvature = 0.35
set: ScreenEffects.Aberration = 0.35
set: ScreenEffects.Grain = 0.3
say: Scanlines, curved glass, color fringes and a little grain make an old TV.
play
wait: 1
hold: Left 1.5
wait: 1.5
stop
set: ScreenEffects.Scanlines = 0
set: ScreenEffects.Curvature = 0
set: ScreenEffects.Aberration = 0
set: ScreenEffects.Grain = 0
set: ScreenEffects.PixelSize = 4
set: ScreenEffects.Palette = GameBoy
explain: field:ScreenEffects.Palette | Palette | Or chunky pixels in four shades of green, like an old handheld. There's sepia and one bit black and white too.
play
wait: 1
hold: Right 1.5
wait: 1.5
stop
explain: component:ScreenEffects | Tween them | Saturation, contrast, brightness and tint grade the colors, and scripts can change any of it as the game runs: drain the color as the player's health runs low.
